🧩 Directory Overview
This repository section contains examples of the expected data organisation required to reproduce the multimodal experiments combining histopathological image analysis, nuclear morphometric 
features, clinical variables, and deep learning models.
Due to ethical restrictions and patient privacy regulations, complete whole-slide images (WSIs) and raw clinical datasets are not publicly available. Therefore, only synthetic or representative 
examples  of patches, masks, and directory structures are provided.

🧩 1. Example Patch and Mask Structure
The following structure illustrates the expected organisation of image patches and segmentation masks used during training, validation, and testing.

├── patches/
│   ├── masks/
│   │   ├── train/
│   │   │   ├── Case_1/mask.png
│   │   │   ├── Case_2/mask.png
│   │   │   └── ...
│   │   │
│   │   ├── val/
│   │   │   ├── Case_1/mask.png
│   │   │   ├── Case_2/mask.png
│   │   │   └── ...
│   │   │
│   │   └── test/
│   │       ├── Case_1/mask.png
│   │       ├── Case_2/mask.png
│   │       └── ...
│   │
│   └── patches/
│       ├── train/
│       │   ├── Case_1/patch.png
│       │   ├── Case_2/patch.png
│       │   └── ...
│       │
│       ├── val/
